# 🚀 GIT + PULL REQUEST (STEP-BY-STEP)

# STEP 1: Open your project folder in VS Code

# STEP 2: Create a file
echo "<h1>Hello World</h1>" > index.html

# STEP 3: Initialize Git (only once)
git init

# STEP 4: Add and Commit
git add .
git commit -m "first commit"

# STEP 5: Connect to GitHub repository
git remote add origin https://github.com/pjjj666/hehehe.git

# STEP 6: Push to GitHub (main branch)
git branch -m main
git push -u origin main

# STEP 7: Create a new branch
git checkout -b feature1

# STEP 8: Make changes (edit file or use below)
echo "<p>This is a new change</p>" >> index.html

# STEP 9: Add and Commit changes
git add .
git commit -m "added new change"

# STEP 10: Push new branch to GitHub
git push origin feature1

# STEP 11: Create Pull Request (on GitHub website)
# Go to: https://github.com/pjjj666/hehehe
# Click: "Compare & pull request"
# Select:
#   Base: main
#   Compare: feature1
# Click: "Create Pull Request"

# STEP 12: Merge Pull Request
# Click: "Merge Pull Request"
# Done 🎉



🟢 STEP 10: Create Pull Request (VERY IMPORTANT)

Go to your repo:
👉 GitHub

Then:

* Click Compare & Pull Request
* Base: main
* Compare: feature1
* Click Create Pull Request

⸻

🟢 STEP 11: Merge PR

* Click Merge Pull Request
* Done 🎉